A||N||2||varnster||How do you hook up an aux oil psi gauge?||||5||
Z||000000||varnster||11-02-2001||10:34 PM||||I just want something more reliable than the<BR>factory gauge,I want a reliable seperate gauge that actualy uses psi not an electrical signal, located on the dash or something, can anyone help me out, I have no idea how to hook one up. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||11-03-2001||10:24 AM||||You can put a "T"- fitting on the line that comes out of the oil filter to the pressure sensor (V-6 engine, don't know about 4 cyl.). For the 4 cyl you can probably put the "T" right under the factory pressure sensor. The aftermarket gauges come with some of the fittings and usually a plastic line that you run to your new gauge.You will have to route this new line so it doesn't get cut or melted. Pick a place to mount your new gauge, hook the plastic line to it, and wire in the gauge lights so they come on with your dash lights. You can use a test light or a volt meter to find the right wires to tap into.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||varnster||11-03-2001||10:42 AM||||Thanks! just not sure where to get the most accurate reading, Thanks again! any brand<BR>gauge you guys recomend?||||reg||14
